WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:06.700
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
on Doctor Who we saw the Daleks for the first

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.680
time again since Peter Capaldi became the
Doctor so I thought it would be fun to do

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:16.930
a video for my favorite first appearances
of characters and things.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:20.880
This year is all about correcting mistakes
of the past, so we will be re-visiting a lot

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:21.880
of classics.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.380
A good example is Coal Hill school.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.650
They made the introduction of Danny Pink and
Clara similar to the way the series introduced

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:32.430
Barbara Wright and Ian Chesterton when we
first saw Coal Hill in Unearthly Child.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.399
So this will be a top 5 of first introductions.

00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:37.680
My Q&amp;A video will post later tonight or early
tomorrow morning depending on which time zone

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.680
you’re in.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.280
So still plenty of time to enter the giveaway.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.970
Starting off with Number 5 - The First Doctor
Lies

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:48.610
The Doctor didn’t start quoting the infamous
rules till later incarnations but one of the

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:52.960
first instances of “The Doctor Lies” was
during Unearthly Child.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.290
Well during Cave of the Skulls which was part
of the first serial.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:01:00.370
The way they organized stories back then was
very different from the way hour long episodes

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:01.370
are written today.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:05.290
While visiting pre-historic times the Doctor
is accosted by a caveman who claims he saw

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.520
him make fire.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.630
But when asked to reproduce in front of everyone
he finds he’s forgotten his matches inside

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:11.680
the TARDIS.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.119
One of the Cavemen cries liar.

00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:18.020
It’s not a Doctor’s Rules moment, but
thematically it’s a moment all about broken

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:22.280
promises, broken trust.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.619
The Caveman who found the Doctor trusted him
to help him and The Doctor failed to produce

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.159
when he was put on the spot.

00:01:28.159 --> 00:01:31.460
Moffat is really good about taking bits and
themes from the past and weaving them into

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:32.720
new stories.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.630
Since there are so many first Doctor references
in the first two episodes and capaldi is correcting

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.630
mistakes of the past.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:41.770
I’m wondering if we’ll continue to see
Capaldi trust issues come up.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:45.421
He wants to be a good man but his nature often
gets the better of him.

00:01:45.421 --> 00:01:48.939
Like when they were inside the Dalek and he
stopped for a moment and marveled at the idea

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:53.540
of a good dalek and completely changed the
mission to explore this new crazy thing unfolding

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:54.540
in front of his eyebrows.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:55.700
Just as side note the first acknowledged instance
of the actual list of Doctor Who rules.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.050
When he specifically says Rule Number 1 was
during the fourth doctor’s run in Ribos

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.050
Experiment.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.050
It was Do Exactly as I say though.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:04.590
Rule Number 1 changed a lot of times but The
Doctor Lies and Don’t Wander off are my

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.590
favorite rules.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:08.679
On to Number 4 - First Instance of The TARDIS
acting like it’s own character

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:13.519
The best most recent example is the Doctor’s
Wife where the TARDIS literally becomes a

00:02:13.519 --> 00:02:15.260
person for a brief period.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.080
But the first time it acted like a character
on the show was during the first doctor’s

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.049
run in the third serial Edge of Destruction.

00:02:21.049 --> 00:02:25.349
While leaving Skaro in the previous serial
“The Daleks” the Doctor hits the fast

00:02:25.349 --> 00:02:27.989
return switch on the TARDIS and it gets stuck.

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:32.099
As a result the TARDIS starts traveling uncontrollably
back to the beginning of time which will cause

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:33.099
it to explode.

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:37.519
The TARIS starts behaving weirdly as a way
to communicate the danger to the Doctor and

00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:38.519
his companions.

00:02:38.519 --> 00:02:42.309
So the story is all about the people trying
to communicate with the TARDIS, figure out

00:02:42.309 --> 00:02:44.969
what’s wrong and fix it before everyone
dies.

00:02:44.969 --> 00:02:51.299
Of all the Missy theories, the TARDIS theory
is probably my favorite, just because of the

00:02:51.299 --> 00:02:52.510
impact it might have on the story.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:03:00.069
I think she’ll really be someone much more
sinister as the TARDIS or the Doctor’s TARDIS,

00:03:00.069 --> 00:03:06.040
seemed like more of a benevolent motherly
force.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.680
Missy seems way more like brainwashed Melody
Pond.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:17.109
Edge of Destruction as a tv story was also
big because it was team bonding episode for

00:03:17.109 --> 00:03:20.139
the Doctor and his companions, which makes
me feel like we’ll see something similar

00:03:20.139 --> 00:03:21.739
when Danny Pink boards the TARDIS.

00:03:21.739 --> 00:03:25.079
They’ll have some internal crisis to overcome,
Danny Pink, Clara and The Doctor will work

00:03:25.079 --> 00:03:28.699
through it and start trusting each other more.

00:03:28.699 --> 00:03:31.169
Number 3 - The Daleks Invade Earth

00:03:31.169 --> 00:03:35.290
This was one of the first big instances of
the series bringing the space battle down

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.309
to earth.

00:03:36.309 --> 00:03:41.829
Previously it had always been the companions
being whisked away by the Doctor Peter Pan

00:03:41.829 --> 00:03:42.829
style.

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:47.272
But now the horrors of space brought the adventure
to them.

00:03:47.272 --> 00:03:51.749
They recreated this scene during Mark Gatiss’
Adventure in Time and Space too for any who

00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:53.069
didn’t see it.

00:03:53.069 --> 00:03:58.129
It also became one of the first times the
Daleks started using the battle cry “Exterminate”.

00:03:58.129 --> 00:04:01.510
Before that they had said Exterminated.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.609
But Exterminate would go on to be the famous
line.

00:04:04.609 --> 00:04:08.159
This was also the first time a companion left
the series.

00:04:08.159 --> 00:04:14.790
Susan, in the context of the story falls in
love with a freedom fighter and rather than

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.229
make her choose between him and her new love.

00:04:17.229 --> 00:04:21.840
The Doctor locks her out of the TARDIS.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.539
I know there’s a lot of rumors about Clara
leaving in the Christmas Special.

00:04:25.539 --> 00:04:28.520
We can talk more about that as we get closer
to the series 8 finale.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:36.270
I mentioned it in an earlier video, but the
finale is also going to pay tribute to another

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:38.860
famous alien invasion from the Second Doctor’s
run.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.360
Number 2 - The First Appearance of The Master

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:45.430
John Simms was my first Master but for a lot
of the fandom, Roger Delgado is still the

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:46.590
biggest version.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.979
Just like Tom Baker is the most famous Doctor.

00:04:49.979 --> 00:04:55.030
He was written into the series during the
third doctor’s run in Terror of the Autons.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:05:01.759
There were other stories that explained what
the Master was doing before Terror and they

00:05:01.759 --> 00:05:03.139
even retconned him into earth’s history
to show that he had been there before the

00:05:03.139 --> 00:05:04.490
third doctor was exiled by the time lords.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:08.610
I know everyone wants to see the character
return, and there are a lot of female master

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:15.699
theories based on Moffat’s comments about
the Master being dead and Missy’s time-lord

00:05:15.699 --> 00:05:16.699
like abilities.

00:05:16.699 --> 00:05:18.500
In the expanded novels and audio drama canon
the story goes that The Master was imprisoned

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:22.229
on another planet but the Time Lords released
him so that he would create havok for The

00:05:22.229 --> 00:05:23.229
Doctor and keep him busy.

00:05:23.229 --> 00:05:24.840
The comics have also retconned the master
so that he ended up crossing paths with the

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:25.840
second doctor.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.020
Even though in the tv series he didn’t debut
till the third doctor’s run.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:30.780
Everyone has their own favorite doctor who
villain, but the master is still moriarty

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.500
to the doctor’s sherlock.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:37.150
And all the Danny Pink, Watson references
make me wonder if Moffat is doing the Missy

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.930
Mistress thing as part of a larger Sherlock
theme.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.010
It might just be a coincidence.

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:46.520
But I love the idea that Moffat would try
to slip a Wholock crossover past us without

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.880
people realizing it.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.599
Maybe that’s what the equations are for.

00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:53.229
The key to the Doctor Who universe crossing
over with the Benedict Cumberbatch Sherlock

00:05:53.229 --> 00:05:56.150
universe?

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:02.509
and my Number 1 first - The First Appearance
of Gallifrey

00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:07.319
This was during the second doctor’s run
in War Games.

00:06:07.319 --> 00:06:11.969
The Doctor has to stop an alien race from
creating a super army to conquer the galaxy.

00:06:11.969 --> 00:06:16.560
The Doctor asks the Time Lords for help but
in doing so, submits himself to sanctions

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.610
for stealing the TARDIS during his first incarnation.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:22.690
The planet isn’t called Gallifrey, just
the Home of the Time Lords.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.080
But it’s the first official time we saw
his home.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:28.509
Part of series 8 is taking the long way round
to the pocket universe where gallifrey is

00:06:28.509 --> 00:06:32.569
located and I’m sure some of you have seen
the spoilery images from the finale.

00:06:32.569 --> 00:06:41.680
So if you want to comment on possible connections
to the second doctor’s final story just

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:44.150
use spoiler tags.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:47.379
Gallifrey as a destination is also rumored
to play a role in series 8 but we don’t

00:06:47.379 --> 00:06:48.379
know how or when.

00:06:48.379 --> 00:06:49.379
I at least think we’ll see it in the finale.

00:06:49.379 --> 00:06:52.639
So I’m wondering if Capaldi or Clara will
ask them for help again at a price.

00:06:52.639 --> 00:06:55.660
Capaldi is staying on for series 9 but Jenna
Coleman is still uncertain.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:59.279
So it’s possible she could be collateral
damage in the conflict of the finale and the

00:06:59.279 --> 00:07:00.639
Missy story.

00:07:00.639 --> 00:07:02.940
Unless missy is a future version of Clara.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:06.939
Then everything gets way more confusing.

00:07:06.939 --> 00:07:11.030
But let me know what your favorite first Doctor
Who moment is.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.099
The first use of a catch phrase, the first
time we saw a monster.

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:16.139
Anytime something was done for the first time.

00:07:16.139 --> 00:07:20.319
Like I said, my Q&amp;A will post later tonight
or tomorrow depending on which time zone you

00:07:20.319 --> 00:07:21.319
live in.

00:07:21.319 --> 00:07:24.669
The giveaway for this week will be open until
I make that video.

00:07:24.669 --> 00:07:30.569
All you have to do to enter the giveaway is
be a subscriber and leave a comment.

00:07:30.569 --> 00:07:34.629
Since next week is Robot of Sherwood I might
make my next bonus video about my favorite

00:07:34.629 --> 00:07:36.310
fictional characters in doctor who history.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:40.430
Like when the show took a fantasy character
from a book and made them a character on the

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.430
show.

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:50.099
But feel free to leave me suggestions for
other bonus video topics.

